# Git Push

## Directives

{{#unbound}}
- Inspect the current branch and remote, confirm the intended commits and destination with the user when unclear, then push without rewriting published history.
{{/unbound}}
{{^unbound}}
- Commit current-change work through {{#recommend}}skill:guide-git-commit{{/recommend}} before pushing.
- If other changed files may not belong to this change, consult the user before
  proceeding. Ask whether to include them or leave them uncommitted.
- For approved additions, use {{#recommend}}skill:guide-git-commit{{/recommend}} again before pushing.
- Push only the resulting selected commits using the selected delivery policy.
{{/unbound}}

